# Wrangler-specific (gitignore-style) file: excludes paths from the static
# assets it uploads for this Worker, even though wrangler.jsonc's
# assets.directory is the whole repo root ("./"). Without this, Wrangler
# scans literally everything under the repo root as a candidate asset --
# including .git's own internal object packs, which is what actually broke
# a deploy once akgcc-extra-data/images/ (see below) pushed one of those
# packs over Workers' 25 MiB-per-asset limit. None of the paths below are
# ever served by this site's own domain to begin with, so excluding them
# isn't just a workaround for that failure -- it's also the correct scope
# for what "the site" actually is.

# Version control internals -- never meant to be served, and the actual
# trigger for the Asset too large deploy failure.
.git/

# GitHub Actions workflow definitions, not site content.
.github/

# The scraper scripts, generated JSON, and mirrored event-art images (see
# akgcc-extra-data/events.py) all live here, but this site's own JS fetches
# them straight from raw.githubusercontent.com (see js/config.js's
# EXTRA_DATA_REPO_RAW_BASE) rather than through this Cloudflare-hosted
# domain -- so none of it needs to be (or should be) uploaded as a Worker
# asset. This is also the single biggest thing in the repo by far, growing
# over time as more event art gets mirrored in.
akgcc-extra-data/

# Source for a separate Cloudflare Worker (the daily cron dispatcher), not
# an asset of this one.
cloudflare/

# This Worker's own code (the /mirror/ route), not a static file to serve.
worker/

# Repo/project bookkeeping, not site content.
LICENSE
README.md
UPSTREAM_README.md
.gitignore
wrangler.jsonc
